Subject: cmake: PD_VERSION_HASH, so an iOS build carries the upstream commit it is

VERSION_HASH is `git rev-parse --short HEAD` in CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR. The iOS port
builds build/src - upstream at UPSTREAM_PIN with this overlay applied, and no
.git - so git walks up and answers with the PORT's repository (5294726 for a
v3.15.1 build). Upstream's netplay (v3.15.x) puts VERSION_HASH in CONNECT, in
LAN/lobby room adverts and in the lobby's room filter, and refuses any player
whose build differs from the host's. Found on the lane-3 simulator joining the
macOS oracle with `--connect 127.0.0.1:27100` (D-104): the UDP connect and
handshake worked and the host answered "The host's build is a8c2ab2d7 and
yours is 5294726 - both need the same build." Without this no iOS or visionOS
player could ever join a desktop room of the same release, or host one for
desktop players.

A cache variable rather than a hard-coded value: scripts/build-ios.sh passes
the first nine characters of UPSTREAM_PIN (netBuildSame() compares prefixes of
at least seven, so the CI's own --short length matches either way). Unset, the
build is exactly upstream's. The other VERSION_HASH readers (title-screen
version string, crash report, GE stage cache key) get the upstream commit too,
which is what they describe.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -118,6 +118,17 @@
   OUTPUT_STRIP_TRAILING_WHITESPACE
 )
 
+# PD_VERSION_HASH (iOS port overlay 0058): the commit this build's GAME is,
+# when the tree being built is not that commit's checkout. The iOS port builds
+# a copy of upstream with its overlay applied and no .git, so the rev-parse
+# above answers with the port's own repository - and netplay refuses every
+# player whose VERSION_HASH differs from the host's ("both need the same
+# build"), so an iOS player could never join a desktop room of the same
+# release, nor host one. build-ios.sh passes the pinned upstream commit.
+if(DEFINED PD_VERSION_HASH AND NOT PD_VERSION_HASH STREQUAL "")
+  set(VERSION_HASH "${PD_VERSION_HASH}")
+endif()
+
 # git branch name
 execute_process(
   COMMAND git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD
